   "text": "\n\n**Reproduction plan (\u226415 lines)**  \n\n1. **Model** \u2013 FITS (Frequency Interpolation Time Series Forecasting) with `individual=False`, `enc_in=7`, `seq_len=360` (paper input length), `pred_len=96`, `cut_freq=106` (computed as `int(seq_len//base_T+1)*H_order+10` with `base_T=24`, `H_order=6`), `length_ratio=(seq_len+pred_len)/seq_len`.  \n\n2. **Hyper\u2011parameters** \u2013 learning rate `lr=0.0005` (start script), batch size `batch_size=128` (the script doubles the commanded `--batch_size` because no augmentation is used), epochs `=50`, patience `=20`, optimizer `Adam` (weight decay\u202f=\u202f0\u202f*(uncertain)*).  \n\n3. **Learning\u2011rate schedule** \u2013 `type3` (`--lradj type3`): lr \u2190 lr\u202f\u00d7\u202f0.95\u207d\u1d49\u1d56\u1d52\u1d9c\u02b0\u207b\u00b9\u207e each epoch.  \n\n4. **Training protocol** \u2013 fit **only** on `data[\"train\"]`; use `data[\"val\"]` for early\u2011stopping checkpoint selection (the final 20\u202f% of validation is withheld for the final unbiased evaluation, but the visible part drives checkpoint choice).  \n\n5. **Normalization inside the model** \u2013 RevIN: subtract temporal mean, divide by \u221a(var\u202f+\u202f1e\u20115) before FFT; after IFFT multiply by \u221a(var) and add mean back.  \n\n6. **Frequency pipeline** \u2013 FFT \u2192 zero\u2011pad frequencies beyond `cut_freq` \u2192 linear complex up\u2011sampler to `int(cut_freq*length_ratio)` \u2192 zero\u2011pad to `(seq_len+pred_len)//2+1` bins \u2192 IFFT \u2192 multiply by `length_ratio`. No DLinear branch (commented out in the source).  \n\n7. **Inference** \u2013 set model to `eval()`, disable gradients; predictor receives a `[L,7]` history, crops it to `seq_len` (or les"
